o when you have the time.<br/>They are not routine activities.<br/>Routine activities are things you do every day or every week."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"2\",\"columns\":\"2\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Free Time Activities\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Routine Activities\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go to the movies<br/>go for a walk<br/>go to a sports game<br/>listen to music<br/>go to a museum<br/>visit an art gallery<br/>go to a music festival\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"study<br/>shop for food<br/>go to school<br/>take the bus<br/>go to the gym<br/>eat  lunch<br/>drive to work\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "strong"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a powerful taste"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't like strong coffee."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you are shopping."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "anyway"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that doesn't matter"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He doesn't like going to the movies, but ask him anyway."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to eat out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have a meal at a restaurant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's eat dinner out at Mario's tonight!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "often"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "many times"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  We often go to the mall."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "a lot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large number of times."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They go to the museum a lot!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "all the time"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "regularly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have sandwiches for lunch all the time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le05ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Expressions of Frequency"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "To talk about how often something happens, you use an expression of frequency. <br/>This can be an adverb like <span class = \"italic\">often</span>, <span class = \"italic\">sometimes</span>, <span class = \"italic\">never</span>.<br/>It can also be expression like <span class = \"italic\">a lot</span>, <span class = \"italic\">all the time</span>, <span class = \"italic\">when I can</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She goes to the mall all the time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He doesn't come here often."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They eat in this restaurant a lot."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le05ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go to your favorite shopping mall or shopping area."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of things you can do there."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find the English words for activities in a dictionary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I